# Coach speech (Danish): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "du" to the player and "jeg" of himself; Danish
# adjectives and participles never agree with a person's gender.
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   definite nouns ("åbningen", "midtspillet", "slutspillet"): "i {text}",
#                       "{text} gik bedst".
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement right after "remis", no comma: "Remis {text}." ("Remis efter
#                       aftale.", "Partiet endte remis ved pat.").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase WITH "at", lower case, no full stop: said after a colon
#                       ("Tema: at holde dine brikker dækket.") or after "husk", "prøv", "øve dig i"
#                       ("Husk at give din konge lidt luft.").
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach level names of the menus (coach.level.N.name) in Danish guillemets,
#                       said after "niveauet" or alone: "klar til niveauet »Begynder«".
# {opening:def} inside a sentence, {opening} alone after a colon.
# Move numbers: "i træk {n}" (cardinal after the noun, glossary). Accuracy: {acc:percent} = "85
# procent" where English says "{acc} percent", the bare number where English has it bare.
# "In a row" is "i streg" in these lines (they all contain "træk" already: "3 gange i streg").

